questions.question_text:
Find the perimeter of this shape, correct to $1$ decimal place.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.85]
\draw (0,0) -- (4.4,0) node[midway,below] {$11\text{ m}$};
\draw (0,2.4) -- (4.4,2.4) node[midway,above] {$11\text{ m}$};
\draw (0,0) -- (0,2.4) node[midway,left] {$6\text{ m}$};
\draw (4.4,2.4) arc[start angle=90,end angle=-90,radius=1.2];
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Calculate the perimeter of this shape, correct to $2$ decimal places.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.9]
\draw (0,2) -- (2.5,2) node[midway,above] {$5\text{ cm}$};
\draw (2.5,2) -- (2.5,0) node[midway,right] {$4\text{ cm}$};
\draw (2.5,0) -- (-2,0) node[midway,below] {$9\text{ cm}$};
\draw (-2,0) arc[start angle=180,end angle=90,radius=2];
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Find the perimeter of this shape, correct to $1$ decimal place.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.8]
\draw (0,0) -- (5,0) node[midway,below] {$25\text{ m}$};
\draw (0,2.8) -- (5,2.8) node[midway,above] {$25\text{ m}$};
\draw (5,2.8) arc[start angle=90,end angle=-90,radius=1.4];
\draw (0,0) arc[start angle=-90,end angle=-270,radius=1.4];
\draw[<->] (-2.1,0) -- (-2.1,2.8) node[midway,left] {$14\text{ m}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

The shape below has a semicircle added on top and an identical semicircle removed from the bottom. Find its perimeter, correct to $2$ decimal places.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.9]
\draw (0,0) -- (0,2.7) node[midway,left] {$9\text{ cm}$};
\draw (1.8,0) -- (1.8,2.7) node[midway,right] {$9\text{ cm}$};
\draw (1.8,2.7) arc[start angle=0,end angle=180,radius=0.9];
\draw (0,0) arc[start angle=180,end angle=0,radius=0.9];
\draw[<->] (0,-0.7) -- (1.8,-0.7) node[midway,below] {$6\text{ cm}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

A quarter circle is cut from the corner of a square of side $10$ mm, as shown. Find the perimeter of the remaining piece, correct to $1$ decimal place.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.9]
\draw (2.6,0) -- (2.6,2.6) node[midway,right] {$10\text{ mm}$};
\draw (2.6,2.6) -- (0,2.6) node[midway,above] {$10\text{ mm}$};
\draw (2.6,0) arc[start angle=0,end angle=90,radius=2.6];
\draw[dashed] (0,0) -- (2.6,0);
\draw[dashed] (0,0) -- (0,2.6);
\fill (0,0) circle (1.5pt);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Give the exact perimeter of this shape, in terms of $\pi$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.85]
\draw (0,0) -- (4.2,0) node[midway,below] {$14\text{ m}$};
\draw (0,2.4) -- (4.2,2.4) node[midway,above] {$14\text{ m}$};
\draw (0,0) -- (0,2.4) node[midway,left] {$8\text{ m}$};
\draw (4.2,2.4) arc[start angle=90,end angle=-90,radius=1.2];
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

The top of this shape is an arc of a circle centred at the midpoint of the base. Find the perimeter, correct to $2$ decimal places.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=1.5]
\coordinate (O) at (0,0);
\draw (-1.6,0) -- (1.6,0) node[midway,below] {$16\text{ cm}$};
\draw (-1.6,0) -- (-1.6,1.2) node[midway,left] {$6\text{ cm}$};
\draw (1.6,0) -- (1.6,1.2) node[midway,right] {$6\text{ cm}$};
\draw (36.87:2) arc[start angle=36.87,end angle=143.13,radius=2];
\draw[dashed] (O) -- (36.87:2);
\draw[dashed] (O) -- (143.13:2);
\draw (36.87:0.6) arc[start angle=36.87,end angle=143.13,radius=0.6];
\node[font=\small] at (0,0.92) {$106.3^{\circ}$};
\node[fill=white,inner sep=1pt,font=\small] at (1.16,0.87) {$10\text{ cm}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

The shape below is a rectangle capped with a semicircle. The capped end measures $8$ m and the whole perimeter is $40$ m. Find the rectangle length $x$, correct to $2$ decimal places.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.85]
\draw (0,0) -- (2.45,0) node[midway,below] {$x$};
\draw (0,2) -- (2.45,2) node[midway,above] {$x$};
\draw (0,0) -- (0,2) node[midway,left] {$8\text{ m}$};
\draw (2.45,2) arc[start angle=90,end angle=-90,radius=1];
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
